    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0558" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72114/4237a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-09T16:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 9, 1918—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>154. Military Attaché, Berne, reports under date of December 5th<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d412-f1"/> critical condition of 20,000 Russian officers now
                    prisoners in Germany. Fear that if they returned to Russia it would mean certain
                    death. Department would like to know whether the matter was being considered by
                    the Supreme War Council and what action if any had been taken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
